<h3 class="text-base font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Privacy Notice</h3>
<p>Welcome to COMPASS, a web based platform for Project Dial-A-Friend.</p>
<p>COMPASS is committed to protecting your privacy in accordance with the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173).</p>
<p>To provide peer-support services, the system collects and processes information such as your anonymous alias, age, gender, screening responses, session records, referrals, and feedback. If you voluntarily provide personally identifiable information (e.g., name, email, contact number, or emergency contact), it will be securely stored in the Identity Vault, which is isolated from operational records and accessible only to authorized personnel under approved circumstances.</p>
<p>During peer-support sessions, Helpers will only see your system-generated anonymous alias and information necessary to provide appropriate support. Personally identifiable information will not be disclosed except with your consent, during approved referrals, emergency situations involving serious risk to life or safety, or when required by law.</p>
<p>Text-chat sessions automatically generate an encrypted transcript as part of the session record. For voice-call sessions, temporary recording and transcript generation require your informed consent. These records are used solely for competency evaluation, Adviser supervision, quality assurance, referral review, emergency verification, incident investigation, and other authorized institutional purposes. They are encrypted, accessible only to authorized personnel, retained in accordance with the approved institutional retention schedule, and securely deleted after the retention period unless continued retention is required by law or an authorized investigation.</p>
<p>If you choose not to consent to voice recording, you may continue receiving peer-support services through the secure text-chat feature. Declining voice-recording consent will not prevent you from accessing peer-support services.</p>
<p>Session summaries and anonymized records may be used for competency monitoring, program evaluation, and institutional reporting while maintaining user confidentiality.</p>
<p>By selecting &quot;I Agree&quot;, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Notice and consent to the collection, processing, storage, and protection of your information for the purposes described above.</p>